; `any` as an array element (`[any]`; equally `{ k: any }` map values) is a SUPPORTED rust position
; under --wasm=false: it lowers to the `AnyCbor` static-runtime type (loose-CBOR A2, rust-only). The
; robustness catalog runs the DEFAULT profile (--wasm=true), where an any-using spec is gracefully
; rejected (the wasm AnyCbor wrapper is phase A3) — so this row is `error (graceful)`, NOT a panic
; (it formerly panicked at the `generic_instances` assert, before `any` had an IR representation).
; The position's rust support is proven by the --wasm=false snapshot/e2e fixtures.
a = [any]
